om/cppinvestments/job/Toronto/Associate--Structured-Credit-Asset-Management_JR00848","source_url":"https://cppib.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/cppinvestments/job/Toronto/Associate--Structured-Credit-Asset-Management_JR00848","source_name":"CPP Investments public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Associate Private Credit opportunity with CPP Investments in Toronto, ON focused on Private Credit.","description_text":"Purpose. Performance. People. Joining CPP Investments means joining one of the world’s most admired and respected institutional investors to drive a single mandate: to deliver strong, sustainable returns for generations of Canadians. With a long-term horizon and global reach, we deploy capital at scale across public and private markets. Our size, stability, and disciplined investment philosophy allow us to pursue complex opportunities and build enduring partnerships worldwide. For our people, this means meaningful work with tangible impact, real opportunity, and collaboration with exceptional colleagues who value partnership and performance. Here, you’ll contribute to outcomes that matter alongside team members committed to excellence and shared success. The Role Reporting to the Managing Director, Credit Asset Management, you will help take CPP Investments’ structured credit platform to the next level by managing a growing portfolio while building the processes and tools that allow us to operate at scale. This role is designed for someone with initiative, curiosity, and ambition to grow as an investment management professional. You will have real ownership of the day-to-day management of our structured credit investments and flow programs, while also being expected to improve how the work gets done. You will use AI, automation, and data tools to redesign manual and repetitive workflows, strengthen controls, and make the platform more scalable. The objective is to spend progressively less time chasing information, checking templates, and manually updating spreadsheets—and more time understanding portfolio performance, identifying risks and opportunities, and developing investment judgment. The role offers an opportunity to build deep expertise in a large structured credit portfolio, help shape how the platform operates, and take on increasingly sophisticated portfolio management responsibilities over time. The Team Credit Asset Management is building next-generation asset management capabilities to support Credit Investments’ growth over the next decade and beyond. The team combines credit expertise with technology, including GenAI, to drive alpha through operational efficiency, risk mitigation, and proprietary insights. The team offers a unique opportunity to work at the intersection of credit analysis, portfolio management and technology, with exposure to CPP Investments’ global credit platform. Accountabilities Own the ongoing management and monitoring of structured credit investments and flow programs across the Americas, developing a deep understanding of each investment’s thesis, structure, economics, risks, and performance drivers. Manage the recurring execution of forward flows, warehouses, asset purchase facilities, securitizations, and related financing structures, including funding, borrowing bases, waterfalls, and transaction reporting. Analyze borrower, servicer, collateral, and transaction data to assess performance against underwriting expectations, identify emerging trends and risks, and develop actionable investment insights. Continuously redesign how the work gets done. Use AI, automation, Python, SQL, and external service providers to eliminate repetitive manual work, improve controls and data quality, and build scalable workflows. Develop clear views on portfolio performance and material developments, communicate them effectively to deal teams and other stakeholders, and proactively identify issues requiring action. Build and improve the monitoring, reporting, analytical, and control infrastructure needed to manage a growing structured credit portfolio efficiently. Partner closely with investment teams and functions across CPP Investments, taking on increasingly sophisticated responsibilities as your knowledge and judgment develop. Qualifications 2-4 years of relevant experience in structured credit, asset-backed finance, or securitized products. Strong understanding of structured credit products and financing structures, with experience in areas such as forward flows, warehouse facilities, asset-backed lending, ABS, CLOs or SRTs. Excellent credit, analytical, and financial modeling skills, with the curiosity to translate analysis into investment conclusions. Demonstrated ability to use AI, Python, SQL, or similar technologies to improve workflows, analyze data, and increase team effectiveness. High degree of ownership and initiative. You identify problems, develop solutions, and drive work forward without waiting for a detailed playbook. Intellectual curiosity and ambition to grow from process execution into increasingly sophisticated portfolio analysis, judgment, and portfolio management responsibility. Strong attention to detail and judgment: automation should reduce manual work without compromising the rigor, controls, and accuracy required to manage institutional capital. Strong communication skills and the ability to turn complex information into clear conclusions, recommendations, and actions. Undergraduate degree in a relevant discipline; progress toward a CFA or CPA designation is an asset. You are motivated to contribute to something larger than yourself, approach complex challenges with rigor, and hold yourself to high standards in a collaborative, performance-driven environment. We provide colleagues with cutting-edge AI tools, dedicated learning time, and practical support to help them deliver with greater impact. Inclusion & Accessibility CPP Investments is committed to equitable access to employment and building a workforce that reflects diverse talent and perspectives. If you require accommodation at any stage of the recruitment process, please let us know and we will work with you to meet your needs. Attention: Protect Yourself from Fraud CPP Investments is committed to a secure and transparent recruitment process. We will never ask candidates for payment or financial information at any stage of hiring. All legitimate opportunities are posted on our careers page, and communications will come from our applicant tracking system, Workday. CPP Investments may use AI tools to help screen and assess applicants by analyzing resumes and applications for relevant skills and experience. These tools support, but do not replace, human decision-making. #LI-ONSITE","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"cpp-investments:JR00848","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"7222","company_id":"ontario-teachers","company_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan","title":"Managing Director – Private Capital, Software","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equity","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Managing Director","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-03","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":255000,"salary_max":275000,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://otppb.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/OntarioTeachers_Careers/job/Toronto-Canada/Managing-Director---Private-Capital--Software_7222","source_url":"https://otppb.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/OntarioTeachers_Careers/job/Toronto-Canada/Managing-Director---Private-Capital--Software_7222","source_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Managing Director Private Equity opportunity with Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan in Toronto, ON focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"Company : Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan Board 160 Front Street West, Suite 3200 Toronto, Ontario M5J 0G4 Job Title : Managing Director – Private Capital, Software NOC : 10021– Banking Credit, and Other Investment Managers Wage : Annual base salary of $255,000-$275,000 (37.5 hours per week) - permanent/full-time Location(s) of work : 160 Front Street West, Suite 3200, Toronto, Ontario, M5J 0G4 Canada Number of Positions : One (1) Required Language Skills : English The Opportunity The Managing Director will be working as an Investment Manager, collaborating with investment professionals with deep sector and regional expertise and will play a key role in making and managing direct investments in the Technology sector. Who you'll work with Reporting to the Senior Managing Director (SMD), the Managing Director will lead deal teams comprising analysts, associates and principals, supported by third party consultants, operating executives, legal and accounting professionals dedicated to each particular investment. In certain instances, the Managing Director may also work with colleagues in the London, Singapore or Mumbai offices in evaluating international investment opportunities in a given sector. Key Responsibilities : Plan, organize and direct investment opportunities within the Technology sector. Manage a team of investment professionals responsible for evaluating, structuring, and executing investments. Establish investment priorities, operational objectives, policies, and procedures to support the organization’s investment mandate and long-term growth strategy. Undertaking analysis of investments, which includes conducting industry and company due diligence, creating sophisticated financial models, arranging debt financing, negotiating legal documents, formulating value creation plans (in partnership with operating teams and other lead investors) and preparing written recommendations. Lead the investment decision-making process by reviewing analyses and recommendations prepared by investment professionals and presenting strategic recommendations to senior leadership and investment committees. Direct negotiations relating to acquisitions, investments, financing arrangements, and other strategic transactions, ensuring alignment with organizational objectives and risk management requirements. Manage relationships with investors, co-investment partners, lenders, advisors, portfolio company executives, and other key stakeholders within the financial services and investment community. Oversee performance of investment portfolio and provide strategic direction to management teams and investment professionals to support operational improvements, growth initiatives, and value creation strategies. Represent the organization on boards of directors and board committees of portfolio companies and provide governance oversight to ensure achievement of strategic and financial objectives. Establish business development and investment origination strategies, identifying new investment opportunities, networking and fostering industry relationships, and expanding the organization's presence within the Technology investment ecosystem. Direct market research initiatives and sector coverage strategies to identify emerging trends, investment opportunities, and risks that may affect investment performance and portfolio management decisions. Oversee the preparation of reports, recommendations, and presentations for senior management, investors, and investment committees. Manage departmental resources, establish performance objectives, and provide leadership, mentorship, and professional development opportunities for investment team members. Collaborate with senior management and global leadership to develop and implement strategic initiatives, investment policies, and operational plans that support the organization's overall business objectives. Ensure compliance with applicable regulatory requirements, internal policies, governance standards, and risk management practices relating to investment activities and portfolio management. Required Skills: The individual will have significant prior expertise and a strong track record investing in Technology, particularly in Software with knowledge of emerging AI and digitization themes. Key focus areas include Application software, Infrastructure software, Digital & IT Services and other Tech-enabled categories. 10+ years of work experience with a substantial track record of private equity deal leadership in investment banking. Track record sponsoring deals at Underwriting / Investment Committee and delivering committed returns across a full investment cycle, including conducting and leading multiple diligence streams (financial, operational, legal, tax, insurance), arranging debt financing, and negotiating documentation. Direct investment track record in Technology is required; Software expertise is particularly valued. Please include your deal sheet with your application. Deep knowledge of Technology sector dynamics and the emerging regulatory, AI, and digitization themes reshaping them Demonstrated leadership across the full investment process, including sourcing, due diligence, debt financing, negotiation, and exit. Strong negotiating skills, with ability to lead commercial terms in acquisitions, mergers, and financings. Ability to balance priorities, work independently, lead teams, and thrive in a high-performance environment. Very strong analytical and quantitative skills to perform and guide in-depth, innovative, critical analysis. Deep understanding of fundamental investment analysis and private equity value creation. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to build constructive relationships with internal and external parties, particularly management teams, boards, and senior advisors. Strong communication skills, both oral and written, including IC paper authorship and presentation. Willingness and ability to travel across North America and globally. Required Education : Undergraduate Degree or Masters Degree in Economics, Commerce, Finance or Business Administration Benefits Pay for performance environment that offers competitive salary and incentives Numerous opportunities for professional growth and development Comprehensive employer paid benefits coverage, including a Health Spending Account Retirement income through a defined benefit pension plan Competitive time off Discount programs including Edvantage and Perkopolis 20 vacation days Bonus (Discretionary Pay for Performance) Other Benefits (Employee Assistance Program) Medical Benefits Dental Benefits Disability Benefits Life Insurance Benefits Group Insurance Benefits Pension Benefits Vision Care Benefits The opportunity to invest back into the fund through our Deferred Incentive Program At Ontario Teachers', diversity is one of our core strengths. We take pride in ensuring that the people we hire and the culture we create, reflect and embrace diversity of thought, background and experience. Through our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion strategy and our Employee Resource Groups (ERGs), we celebrate diversity and foster inclusion through events for colleagues to connect for professional development, networking & mentoring. We are building an inclusive and equitable workplace where our talent is respected, accepted and empowered to be themselves. To learn more about our commitment to Diversity, Equity and Inclusion, check out Life at Teachers'. How to Apply : Are you ready to pursue new challenges and take your career to the next level? Apply today! Please send your resume to the following email address: Job_Application@otpp.com and reference Requisition #7222. Attention: Eryn O'Shaughnessy You may be invited to complete a pre-recorded interview as part of the recruitment process. This will take no longer than 10 minutes. Accommodations are available upon request (peopleandculture@otpp.com) for candidates with a disability taking part in the recruitment process and once hired. Ontario Teachers’ may use AI-based tools to assist in screening and assessing applicants for this position. These tools may help us identify candidates whose skills and experience align with Ontario Teachers’ objectives by analyzing information provided in resumes and applications. Our use of AI does not replace human decision-making. We thank you for applying and look forward to reviewing your application. #LI-OTPP #LI-LE1","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"ontario-teachers:7222","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"7004","company_id":"ontario-teachers","company_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan","title":"Managing Director, Financial Services, Private Capital","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equity","specialization":"Private Equity","seniority":"Managing Director","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-05-07","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://otppb.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/OntarioTeachers_Careers/job/Toronto-Canada/Managing-Director--Financial-Services--Private-Capital_7004","source_url":"https://otppb.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/OntarioTeachers_Careers/job/Toronto-Canada/Managing-Director--Financial-Services--Private-Capital_7004","source_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Managing Director Private Equity opportunity with Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan in Toronto, ON focused on Private Equity.","description_text":"The opportunity Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan Board (Ontario Teachers') is a global investor with net assets of ~$279 billion as of December 31, 2025. Ontario Teachers’ is a fully funded defined benefit pension plan, and it invests in a broad array of asset classes to deliver retirement security for 346,000 working members and pensioners. Our Private Capital group deploys ~$60 billion across direct private equity investments and private equity funds globally. The Managing Director will lead investments end-to-end — from origination through exit — sponsor transactions at Underwriting Committee, take active board roles at portfolio companies, and help build and develop the Financial Services investment team. This is a senior seat for a candidate with a proven private equity track record and deep Financial Services expertise. Who you'll work with Reporting to the Senior Managing Director, the role will be part of a deal team comprising analysts, associates, principals, directors, and managing directors, supported by third-party consultants, operating executives, and legal and accounting advisors dedicated to each transaction. The Financial Services team invests across sub-sectors including Insurance, Wealth & Asset Management, Lending, Professional Services, and Cards & Payments, with particular need to understand the regulatory, AI, and digitization themes reshaping the sector. The role will also potentially partner with colleagues in OTPP's global offices on international investment and / or cross asset class opportunities in Financial Services. What you'll do Lead deal teams end-to-end, from origination through close and through the life of the investment; serve as the named sponsor at Underwriting Committee and author Underwriting Committee papers. Own deal execution with limited oversight — including pricing, structuring, financing, and final commercial and legal negotiating positions. Take active board leadership roles at portfolio companies; drive value creation agendas with management and sponsor follow-on capital, M&A, and exit decisions. Originate proprietary deal flow through personal networks with CEOs, operating executives, sponsors, bankers, and advisors; represent OTPP Financial Services externally. Set coverage priorities and investment theses for one or more sub-sectors; partner with the SMDs on team strategy and sector positioning. Build, lead, and develop the Financial Services investment team; partner with the SMDs on hiring, performance management, and succession. Hold the team accountable for quality of judgment, execution discipline, and alignment with OTPP's mission, vision, and values. Work in a highly collaborative manner, bringing a complex network of stakeholders along (Global and Sector SMDs, deal teams, Portfolio Solutions / Value Creation, international office leaders, portfolio companies). Strike the appropriate balance of being a confident decision-maker and an inclusive leader. Define value creation playbooks across the Financial Services portfolio and hold portfolio company management accountable for delivery. Exercise independent judgment on deal execution within approved mandates; serve as the named sponsor at Underwriting Committee and hold board-level decision authority at portfolio companies. Provide disciplined thinking, sound judgment, and courage of conviction, with a willingness to take balanced, thesis-driven risk. This includes stepping in and intervening directly and effectively when required. What you'll need ~15+ years of meaningful work experience with a substantial track record of private equity deal leadership. Supplementary experience in management consulting, investment banking, and/or corporate M&A (preferably corporate development or similar) considered in combination with PE tenure. Track record sponsoring deals at Underwriting / Investment Committee and delivering committed returns across a full investment cycle, including conducting and leading multiple diligence streams (financial, operational, legal, tax, insurance), arranging debt financing, and negotiating documentation. Direct investment track record in Financial Services required; insurance, wealth, or payments expertise particularly valued. Deep knowledge of Financial Services sector dynamics — particularly Insurance, Wealth & Asset Management, Lending, Professional Services, and Cards & Payments — and the emerging regulatory, AI, and digitization themes reshaping them. Active “for profit” board director experience, including committee leadership. Strong academic background, with a financial designation (MBA, CFA, CBV, or CA strongly preferred). Demonstrated leadership across the full investment process, including sourcing, due diligence, debt financing, negotiation, and exit. Strong negotiating skills, with ability to lead commercial terms in acquisitions, mergers, and financings. Ability to balance priorities, work independently, lead teams, and thrive in a high-performance environment. Very strong analytical and quantitative skills to perform and guide in-depth, innovative, critical analysis. Deep understanding of fundamental investment analysis and private equity value creation. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to build constructive relationships with internal and external parties, particularly management teams, boards, and senior advisors. Strong communication skills, both oral and written, including IC paper authorship and presentation. Willingness and ability to travel across North America and globally. #LI-EO1 What we’re offering Numerous opportunities for professional growth and development Comprehensive employer paid benefits coverage Retirement income through a defined benefit pension plan The opportunity to invest back into the fund through our Deferred Incentive Program A flexible work environment combining in office collaboration and remote working Competitive time off Our Flexible Travel Program gives you the option to work abroad in another region/country for up to a month each year Employee discount programs including Edvantage and Perkopolis At Ontario Teachers', diversity is one of our core strengths. We take pride in ensuring that the people we hire and the culture we create, reflect and embrace diversity of thought, background and experience. Through our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion strategy and our Employee Resource Groups (ERGs), we celebrate diversity and foster inclusion through events for colleagues to connect for professional development, networking & mentoring. We are building an inclusive and equitable workplace where our talent is respected, accepted and empowered to be themselves. To learn more about our commitment to Diversity, Equity and Inclusion, check out Life at Teachers'. How to apply Are you ready to pursue new challenges and take your career to the next level? Apply today! You may be invited to complete a pre-recorded digital interview as part of your application. Accommodations are available upon request (peopleandculture@otpp.com) for candidates with a disability taking part in the recruitment process and once hired. Candidates must be legally entitled to work in the country where this role is located. Ontario Teachers’ may use AI-based tools to assist in screening and assessing applicants for this position. These tools may help us identify candidates whose skills and experience align with Ontario Teachers’ objectives by analyzing information provided in resumes and applications. Our use of AI does not replace human decision-making. To learn more about how Teachers’ uses AI with your personal information, please visit our Privacy Centre. Functional Areas: Investments Vacancy: Current Requisition ID: 7004 #LI-EO1","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"ontario-teachers:7004","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"7008","company_id":"ontario-teachers","company_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan","title":"Director, Private Capital, Services","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equity","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Director","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-05-07","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://otppb.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/OntarioTeachers_Careers/job/Toronto-Canada/Director--Private-Capital--Services_7008","source_url":"https://otppb.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/OntarioTeachers_Careers/job/Toronto-Canada/Director--Private-Capital--Services_7008","source_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Director Private Equity opportunity with Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan in Toronto, ON focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"The opportunity Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan Board (Ontario Teachers') is a global investor with net assets of ~$279 billion as of December 31, 2025. Ontario Teachers’ is a fully funded defined benefit pension plan, and it invests in a broad array of asset classes to deliver retirement security for 346,000 working members and pensioners. Our Private Capital group deploys ~$60 billion across direct private equity investments and private equity funds globally. The Director will be a senior member of our Services investment team – partnering with our Senior Managing Director and Managing Directors to source, diligence, execute, and manage private investments in the Services sector. This is a development seat with a clear path toward independent deal leadership for a candidate who has already built a strong foundation in private equity investing. Who you'll work with Reporting to the Managing Director, the role will be part of a deal team comprising analysts, associates, principals, directors, and managing directors, supported by third-party consultants, operating executives, and legal and accounting advisors dedicated to each transaction. The Services team invests across sub-sectors including Commercial & Residential Services and Industrial & Infrastructure Services. The Managing Director should have prior expertise in Services investing, with knowledge of emerging regulatory, AI, and digitization themes that are reshaping the sector. In certain instances, the Director may also work with colleagues in OTPP's global offices on international investment opportunities in Services. What you'll do Serve as a key member of deal teams — conducting industry and company due diligence, building financial models, arranging debt financing, negotiating legal documents, and preparing written recommendations for the Underwriting Committee. Lead or co-lead individual deals and workstreams with oversight from the SMD or MD; own specific diligence streams (financial, operational, commercial, legal, tax, insurance) end-to-end. Post-close, remain actively involved with portfolio companies — often as board observer or board member — working with management on strategy, value creation, M&A, and refinancing. Contribute to deal flow generation through desk research, consultant relationships, operating executive networks, conferences, and relationships with management teams. Lead sub-sector deep dives and thematic research as the team evolves its coverage strategy, including emerging AI, regulatory, and digitization themes. Manage and develop analysts, associates, and principals on deal teams; provide direct mentorship on diligence, modeling, judgment, and communication. Work in a highly collaborative manner, bringing a complex network of stakeholders along (Global and Sector SMDs, MDs, deal teams, Portfolio Solutions team, international office leaders, portfolio companies, etc.). Strike the appropriate balance of being a confident decision-maker and an inclusive leader. Build a network of operating executives, CEOs, consultants, bankers, and peer sponsors; progress toward independent deal sourcing by the end of Director tenure. Develop value creation expertise in close partnership with the SMD and MDs; contribute to portfolio company initiatives as assigned. Exercise judgment within deal teams and surface recommendations to the MD or SMD; lead individual workstreams and, over time, full deals with oversight. Provide disciplined thinking, sound judgment, and courage of conviction, with a willingness to take balanced, thesis-driven risk. Intervene directly and effectively when required and escalate issues early. Work cross-functionally and collaboratively with other teams to ensure continued alignment with OTPP's mission, vision, and values — including supporting and sharing knowledge with other areas of Investments and responding to ad hoc requests. What you'll need ~10+ years of meaningful work experience, including several years of recent private equity investing. Active M&A in a senior role in corporate development would also be considered. Supplemented by previous experience in management consulting, investment banking, and/or corporations (preferably corporate development or similar roles). Experience playing a lead role on deal workstreams, including conducting due diligence, leading multiple diligence streams (financial, operational, legal, tax, insurance), arranging debt financing, and negotiating documentation. Direct investment exposure to Services sub-sectors preferred. Deep knowledge of Services sector dynamics and the emerging regulatory, AI, and digitization themes reshaping them. Some experience serving on “for profit” Boards of Directors or board committees a plus. Strong academic background, with a financial designation (MBA, CFA, CBV, or CA strongly preferred). Experience playing a leading role in the investment process, including conducting due diligence, arranging debt financing, and negotiating documentation. Strong negotiating skills. Ability to balance priorities, work independently, lead projects, and thrive in a high-performance team environment. Very strong analytical and quantitative skills to perform and guide in-depth, innovative, critical analysis. Deep understanding of fundamental investment analysis and private equity value creation. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to build constructive relationships with internal and external parties, particularly management teams, boards, and senior advisors. Strong communication skills, both oral and written, including IC paper authorship and presentation. Willingness and ability to travel across North America and globally. #LI-EO1 What we’re offering Numerous opportunities for professional growth and development Comprehensive employer paid benefits coverage Retirement income through a defined benefit pension plan The opportunity to invest back into the fund through our Deferred Incentive Program A flexible work environment combining in office collaboration and remote working Competitive time off Our Flexible Travel Program gives you the option to work abroad in another region/country for up to a month each year Employee discount programs including Edvantage and Perkopolis At Ontario Teachers', diversity is one of our core strengths. We take pride in ensuring that the people we hire and the culture we create, reflect and embrace diversity of thought, background and experience. Through our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion strategy and our Employee Resource Groups (ERGs), we celebrate diversity and foster inclusion through events for colleagues to connect for professional development, networking & mentoring. We are building an inclusive and equitable workplace where our talent is respected, accepted and empowered to be themselves. To learn more about our commitment to Diversity, Equity and Inclusion, check out Life at Teachers'. How to apply Are you ready to pursue new challenges and take your career to the next level? Apply today! You may be invited to complete a pre-recorded digital interview as part of your application. Accommodations are available upon request (peopleandculture@otpp.com) for candidates with a disability taking part in the recruitment process and once hired. Candidates must be legally entitled to work in the country where this role is located. Ontario Teachers’ may use AI-based tools to assist in screening and assessing applicants for this position. These tools may help us identify candidates whose skills and experience align with Ontario Teachers’ objectives by analyzing information provided in resumes and applications. Our use of AI does not replace human decision-making. To learn more about how Teachers’ uses AI with your personal information, please visit our Privacy Centre. Functional Areas: Investments Vacancy: Current Requisition ID: 7008 #LI-EO1","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"ontario-teachers:7008","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"7006","company_id":"ontario-teachers","company_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan","title":"Director, Private Capital, Financial Services","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equit