 tenure. Develop value creation expertise in close partnership with the SMD and MDs; contribute to portfolio company initiatives as assigned. Exercise judgment within deal teams and surface recommendations to the MD or SMD; lead individual workstreams and, over time, full deals with oversight. Provide disciplined thinking, sound judgment, and courage of conviction, with a willingness to take balanced, thesis-driven risk. Intervene directly and effectively when required and escalate issues early. Work cross-functionally and collaboratively with other teams to ensure continued alignment with OTPP's mission, vision, and values — including supporting and sharing knowledge with other areas of Investments and responding to ad hoc requests. What you'll need ~10+ years of meaningful work experience, including several years of recent private equity investing. Active M&A in a senior role in corporate development would also be considered. Supplemented by previous experience in management consulting, investment banking, and/or corporations (preferably corporate development or similar roles). Experience playing a lead role on deal workstreams, including conducting due diligence, leading multiple diligence streams (financial, operational, legal, tax, insurance), arranging debt financing, and negotiating documentation. Direct investment exposure to Financial Services preferred. Familiarity with Financial Services sector dynamics — particularly Insurance, Wealth & Asset Management, Lending, Professional Services, and Cards & Payments — and the regulatory, AI, and digitization themes reshaping them Some experience serving on “for profit” Boards of Directors or board committees a plus. Strong academic background, with a financial designation (MBA, CFA, CBV, or CA strongly preferred). Experience playing a leading role in the investment process, including conducting due diligence, arranging debt financing, and negotiating documentation. Strong negotiating skills. Ability to balance priorities, work independently, lead projects, and thrive in a high-performance team environment. Very strong analytical and quantitative skills to perform and guide in-depth, innovative, critical analysis. Deep understanding of fundamental investment analysis and private equity value creation. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to build constructive relationships with internal and external parties, particularly management teams, boards, and senior advisors. Strong communication skills, both oral and written, including IC paper authorship and presentation. Willingness and ability to travel across North America and globally. #LI-EO1 What we’re offering Numerous opportunities for professional growth and development Comprehensive employer paid benefits coverage Retirement income through a defined benefit pension plan The opportunity to invest back into the fund through our Deferred Incentive Program A flexible work environment combining in office collaboration and remote working Competitive time off Our Flexible Travel Program gives you the option to work abroad in another region/country for up to a month each year Employee discount programs including Edvantage and Perkopolis At Ontario Teachers', diversity is one of our core strengths. We take pride in ensuring that the people we hire and the culture we create, reflect and embrace diversity of thought, background and experience. Through our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion strategy and our Employee Resource Groups (ERGs), we celebrate diversity and foster inclusion through events for colleagues to connect for professional development, networking & mentoring. We are building an inclusive and equitable workplace where our talent is respected, accepted and empowered to be themselves. To learn more about our commitment to Diversity, Equity and Inclusion, check out Life at Teachers'. How to apply Are you ready to pursue new challenges and take your career to the next level? Apply today! You may be invited to complete a pre-recorded digital interview as part of your application. Accommodations are available upon request (peopleandculture@otpp.com) for candidates with a disability taking part in the recruitment process and once hired. Candidates must be legally entitled to work in the country where this role is located. Ontario Teachers’ may use AI-based tools to assist in screening and assessing applicants for this position. These tools may help us identify candidates whose skills and experience align with Ontario Teachers’ objectives by analyzing information provided in resumes and applications. Our use of AI does not replace human decision-making. To learn more about how Teachers’ uses AI with your personal information, please visit our Privacy Centre. Functional Areas: Investments Vacancy: Current Requisition ID: 7006 #LI-EO1","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"ontario-teachers:7006","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"7007","company_id":"ontario-teachers","company_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan","title":"Managing Director, Services, Private Capital","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Equity","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Managing Director","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-05-07","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://otppb.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/OntarioTeachers_Careers/job/Toronto-Canada/Managing-Director--Services--Private-Capital_7007","source_url":"https://otppb.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/OntarioTeachers_Careers/job/Toronto-Canada/Managing-Director--Services--Private-Capital_7007","source_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Managing Director Private Equity opportunity with Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan in Toronto, ON focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"The opportunity Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan Board (Ontario Teachers') is a global investor with net assets of ~$279 billion as of December 31, 2025. Ontario Teachers’ is a fully funded defined benefit pension plan, and it invests in a broad array of asset classes to deliver retirement security for 346,000 working members and pensioners. Our Private Capital group deploys ~$60 billion across direct private equity investments and private equity funds globally. The Managing Director will lead investments end-to-end — from origination through exit — sponsor transactions at Underwriting Committee, take active board roles at portfolio companies, and help build and develop the Services investment team. This is a senior seat for a candidate with a proven private equity track record and deep Services expertise. Who you'll work with Reporting to the Senior Managing Director, the role will be part of a deal team comprising analysts, associates, principals, directors, and managing directors, supported by third-party consultants, operating executives, and legal and accounting advisors dedicated to each transaction. The Services team invests across sub-sectors including Commercial & Residential Services and Industrial & Infrastructure Services. The Managing Director should have prior expertise in Services investing, with knowledge of emerging regulatory, AI, and digitization themes that are reshaping the sector. In certain instances, the Managing Director may also work with colleagues in OTPP's global offices on international investment opportunities in Services. What you'll do Lead deal teams end-to-end, from origination through close and through the life of the investment; serve as the named sponsor at Underwriting Committee and author Underwriting Committee papers. Own deal execution with limited oversight — including pricing, structuring, financing, and final commercial and legal negotiating positions. Take active board leadership roles at portfolio companies; drive value creation agendas with management and sponsor follow-on capital, M&A, and exit decisions. Originate differentiated deal flow through personal networks with CEOs, operating executives, sponsors, bankers, and advisors; represent OTPP Services externally. Set coverage priorities and investment theses for one or more sub-sectors; partner with the SMDs on team strategy and sector positioning. Build, lead, and develop the Services investment team; partner with the SMD on hiring, performance management, and succession. Hold the team accountable for quality of judgment, execution discipline, and alignment with OTPP's mission, vision, and values. Work in a highly collaborative manner, bringing a complex network of stakeholders along (Global and Sector SMDs, deal teams, Portfolio Solutions / Value Creation, international office leaders, portfolio companies). Strike the appropriate balance of being a confident decision-maker and an inclusive leader. Define value creation playbooks across the Services portfolio and hold portfolio company management accountable for delivery. Lead or Co-Lead deals with oversight from SMD, Services team. Exercise independent judgment on deal execution within approved mandates; serve as the named sponsor at Underwriting Committee and hold board-level decision authority at portfolio companies. Provide disciplined thinking, sound judgment, and courage of conviction, with a willingness to take balanced, thesis-driven risk. This includes stepping in and intervening directly and effectively when required. What you'll need ~15+ years of meaningful work experience with a substantial track record of private equity deal leadership. Supplementary experience in management consulting, investment banking, and/or corporate M&A (preferably corporate development or similar) considered in combination with PE tenure. Track record sponsoring deals at Underwriting / Investment Committee and delivering committed returns across a full investment cycle, including conducting and leading multiple diligence streams (financial, operational, legal, tax, insurance), arranging debt financing, and negotiating documentation. Direct investment track record in Services is required; Commercial & Residential Services and Industrial & Infrastructure Services expertise particularly valued. Deep knowledge of Services sector dynamics and the emerging regulatory, AI, and digitization themes reshaping them Active “for profit” board director experience, including committee leadership. Strong academic background, with a financial designation (MBA, CFA, CBV, or CA strongly preferred). Demonstrated leadership across the full investment process, including sourcing, due diligence, debt financing, negotiation, and exit. Strong negotiating skills, with ability to lead commercial terms in acquisitions, mergers, and financings. Ability to balance priorities, work independently, lead teams, and thrive in a high-performance environment. Very strong analytical and quantitative skills to perform and guide in-depth, innovative, critical analysis. Deep understanding of fundamental investment analysis and private equity value creation. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to build constructive relationships with internal and external parties, particularly management teams, boards, and senior advisors. Strong communication skills, both oral and written, including IC paper authorship and presentation. Willingness and ability to travel across North America and globally. #LI-EO1 What we’re offering Numerous opportunities for professional growth and development Comprehensive employer paid benefits coverage Retirement income through a defined benefit pension plan The opportunity to invest back into the fund through our Deferred Incentive Program A flexible work environment combining in office collaboration and remote working Competitive time off Our Flexible Travel Program gives you the option to work abroad in another region/country for up to a month each year Employee discount programs including Edvantage and Perkopolis At Ontario Teachers', diversity is one of our core strengths. We take pride in ensuring that the people we hire and the culture we create, reflect and embrace diversity of thought, background and experience. Through our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion strategy and our Employee Resource Groups (ERGs), we celebrate diversity and foster inclusion through events for colleagues to connect for professional development, networking & mentoring. We are building an inclusive and equitable workplace where our talent is respected, accepted and empowered to be themselves. To learn more about our commitment to Diversity, Equity and Inclusion, check out Life at Teachers'. How to apply Are you ready to pursue new challenges and take your career to the next level? Apply today! You may be invited to complete a pre-recorded digital interview as part of your application. Accommodations are available upon request (peopleandculture@otpp.com) for candidates with a disability taking part in the recruitment process and once hired. Candidates must be legally entitled to work in the country where this role is located. Ontario Teachers’ may use AI-based tools to assist in screening and assessing applicants for this position. These tools may help us identify candidates whose skills and experience align with Ontario Teachers’ objectives by analyzing information provided in resumes and applications. Our use of AI does not replace human decision-making. To learn more about how Teachers’ uses AI with your personal information, please visit our Privacy Centre. Functional Areas: Investments Vacancy: Current Requisition ID: 7007 #LI-EO1","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"ontario-teachers:7007","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"7225","company_id":"ontario-teachers","company_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan","title":"Associate, Infrastructure & Natural Resources - Metals & Mining","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Associate","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-08-28","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://otppb.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/OntarioTeachers_Careers/job/Toronto-Canada/Associate--Infrastructure---Natural-Resources---Metals---Mining_7225-1","source_url":"https://otppb.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/OntarioTeachers_Careers/job/Toronto-Canada/Associate--Infrastructure---Natural-Resources---Metals---Mining_7225-1","source_name":"Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Associate Institutional Investing opportunity with Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan in Toronto, ON focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"The opportunity As an Associate, you will have a key role in analyzing potential Infrastructure & Natural Resources \"INR\" equity investment opportunities, executing transactions and working with existing portfolio companies to craft strategy and implement value-enhancing initiatives. If you are an excellent teammate, highly motivated, and have a desire to travel internationally while working on multiple projects in a fast-paced environment - this is the job for you. Who you'll work with You will be joining our Toronto office, where you will work in a dynamic team-based environment, directly supporting senior team members across multiple sectors and geographic regions, with a focus on Metals & Mining. This is a chance to define and differentiate yourself as an investor and build strategic relationships within the global market. INR consists of a team of over 60 highly-specialized private equity investment professionals, with offices in Toronto, London, Singapore, and an additional presence in Santiago, Chile. Currently, INR leads a geographically diverse portfolio of approximately C$28 billion with assets in North America, South America, Europe, the Middle East, Asia, Australia and New Zealand, and a target to grow to over $40 billion over the next 5 years. The Natural Resources team (which this opportunity supports), targets exposure to commodities in the oil and gas, mining, agriculture, timberland, aquaculture, and other resource-based sectors to provide cash flow, inflation protection and diversification. What you'll do Lead all aspects of the construction and implementation of financial modeling tools to analyze investment opportunities, in conjunction with our Analysts; Assist in the due diligence process and incorporate the findings into a financial model; Deliver high-quality analysis which identifies key value drivers and financial risks through sensitivity and scenario analysis; Coordinate and work closely with external advisors, consultants and partners and submit bids adhering to timelines; Prepare presentations, reports, and investment recommendations to senior management and, where applicable, the Board of OTPP; Review and analyze financial reports, budgets, board books and other information prepared by management of our portfolio companies; Work with portfolio company management to maintain financial models that are used to analyze strategic issues and value the company; Support internal strategic projects, and; Support the preparation of internal annual valuations. What you'll need Minimum of 3 years of experience, preferably in investment banking, principal investing or corporate development within an operating business Bachelor’s degree required, with the pursuit of a CFA designation considered a plus Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to influence others and comfort presenting to senior audiences Excellent analytical and quantitative skills and ability to perform in-depth analysis Ability to balance multiple priorities while remaining detail oriented A proactive attitude and drive toward action and results Advanced skills in Excel and PowerPoint Desire and willingness to travel internationally #LI-JF1 What we’re offering Numerous opportunities for professional growth and development Comprehensive employer paid benefits coverage Retirement income through a defined benefit pension plan The opportunity to invest back into the fund through our Deferred Incentive Program A flexible work environment combining in office collaboration and remote working Competitive time off Our Flexible Travel Program gives you the option to work abroad in another region/country for up to a month each year Employee discount programs including Edvantage and Perkopolis At Ontario Teachers', diversity is one of our core strengths. We take pride in ensuring that the people we hire and the culture we create, reflect and embrace diversity of thought, background and experience. Through our Diversity, Equity and Inclusion strategy and our Employee Resource Groups (ERGs), we celebrate diversity and foster inclusion through events for colleagues to connect for professional development, networking & mentoring. We are building an inclusive and equitable workplace where our talent is respected, accepted and empowered to be themselves. To learn more about our commitment to Diversity, Equity and Inclusion, check out Life at Teachers'. How to apply Are you ready to pursue new challenges and take your career to the next level? Apply today! You may be invited to complete a pre-recorded digital interview as part of your application. Accommodations are available upon request (peopleandculture@otpp.com) for candidates with a disability taking part in the recruitment process and once hired. Candidates must be legally entitled to work in the country where this role is located. Ontario Teachers’ may use AI-based tools to assist in screening and assessing applicants for this position. These tools may help us identify candidates whose skills and experience align with Ontario Teachers’ objectives by analyzing information provided in resumes and applications. Our use of AI does not replace human decision-making. To learn more about how Teachers’ uses AI with your personal information, please visit our Privacy Centre. Functional Areas: Investments Vacancy: Current Requisition ID: 7225 #LI-JF1","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"ontario-teachers:7225","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR101582","company_id":"bci","company_name":"BCI","title":"Private Debt Co-op/Internship (Winter 2027 or Summer 2027)","location_display":"Victoria, BC","city":"Victoria","province":"BC","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Private Credit","specialization":"Private Credit","seniority":"Intern","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Co-op","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-17","application_deadline":"2026-10-02","salary_min":71370,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://bci.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/BCI_Careers/job/Victoria-BC/Private-Debt-Co-op-Internship--Winter-2027-or-Summer-2027-_JR101582","source_url":"https://bci.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/BCI_Careers/job/Victoria-BC/Private-Debt-Co-op-Internship--Winter-2027-or-Summer-2027-_JR101582","source_name":"BCI public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Co-op Intern Private Credit opportunity with BCI in Victoria, BC focused on Private Credit.","description_text":"Closing date: October 1, 2026 Use your research and investment skills in a fast-growing company where you can have an impact. The British Columbia Investment Management Corporation (BCI) is currently seeking Private Debt Co-ops/Interns for the Winter 2027 (January to April) and Summer 2027 (May to August) work terms to provide support across a range of credit investment types, including senior and subordinated debt. WHAT YOU NEED TO KNOW BCI manages a globally diversified portfolio of assets valued at $313.7 billion and is one of Canada’s largest institutional investors. We invest globally to support pension and other funds for more than 30 clients based in British Columbia. We are proud to have been chosen as one of Canada’s Top 100 Employers and BC’s Top Employers . These national and provincial competitions recognize employers who offer exceptional workplaces for their employees. The Private Debt Co-op/Intern will work within our Capital Markets & Credit Investments department. This is a great opportunity for you to learn and apply your knowledge to support the development and implementation of BCI’s Principal Credit Fund, by assisting in the due diligence of new investments, ongoing monitoring of existing investments, and other ad-hoc projects. WHO YOU WILL WORK WITH The Private Debt Team specializes in loans to principally private companies and other specialized credit strategies. Investments primarily consist of direct senior and subordinated debt or co-investments through our partners across a variety of industries in North America, Europe and APAC. WHAT YOU WILL BE DOING Working under the supervision of members of the Private Debt team to assist with various projects Work as an integrated part of the Private Debt team supporting the diligence of prospective investments Assist the Private Debt team in executing new investment opportunities (including comprehensive written reports and financial modeling) Monitor portfolio investments identifying relevant risks Ad-hoc projects and tasks as assigned by the team REQUIRED SKILLS Students in an undergraduate program with a preference for those in Business (Finance or Accounting) or Economics Passion for investing, drive to continually learn about financial markets, and an interest in credit markets Ability to communicate clearly and concisely, both verbally and in writing Ability to meet deadlines while maintaining accuracy, excellent product quality, and attention to detail A high level of professionalism and interpersonal skills Strong research skills combined with analytical and critical thinking and problem-solving abilities A fundamental knowledge of finance, accounting, business, and investment-related disciplines Experience in developing financial models is considered an asset High level of proficiency with Excel, PowerPoint, Word, and Outlook; Bloomberg and S&P Capital IQ/Market Intelligence experience is an asset WHAT WE OFFER Excellent career development and training Work with a dynamic team in a fast-paced environment The development of real-world skills at one of the largest institutional investors in Canada Exposure to some of the most talented, approachable, and inspiring people in the industry The ability to opt-in for access to Dialogue, a user-friendly app that offers virtual primary care, employee and family services, and mental health supports Time to connect with Co-ops/Interns at BCI – build your network and shared learning Two paid days per year for volunteering Competitive pay: $2,745.00 gross bi-weekly + vacation leave paid based on 6% of salary Travel: if coming to Victoria for this work term, BCI will provide a fixed-rate travel allowance based on your location THE DETAILS Work terms: Winter (January to April) 2027 and Summer (May to August) 2027 Department: Capital Markets & Credit Investments Office Location: 750 Pandora Avenue, Victoria, BC Spend your off hours exploring beautiful Victoria and Vancouver Island All co-ops/internships will need to be completed in person at our Victoria office with the option to work one day per week from home. Please note, some positions are not eligible for hybrid work. HOW TO APPLY Apply directly to the Private Debt Co-op/Internship posting on our careers page https://bci.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/BCI_Careers Application deadline: October 1, 2026 at 11:59 pm PDT Please upload a cover letter, resume, and transcripts (unofficial transcript will suffice) Note: We welcome applications from all qualified candidates who are interested in applying for this role. You will need to be legally authorized to work in the country where this job is located. If you currently do not have authorization or if your work permit, study permit, or visa has restrictions or is due to expire during the work term, you may not be eligible for this opportunity. At BCI, we value diversity and believe in fostering an inclusive culture where all employees can be successful. We are performance and client focused and value integrity; if you share these values, we want to know you. We recognize that some skills can be learned on the job and encourage all to apply. If you require an accommodation for the recruitment process (including alternate formats of materials, accessible meeting rooms or other accommodations), contact us at co-op@bci.ca . We would like to hear from you!","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"bci:JR101582","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR101589","company_id":"bci","company_name":"BCI","title":"Analyst, Early Talent Program, Infrastructure & Renewable Resources","location_display":"Victoria, BC","city":"Victoria","province":"BC","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Analyst","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-08","application_deadline":"2026-10-09","salary_min":97000,"salary_max":115000,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://bci.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/BCI_Careers/job/Victoria-BC/Analyst--Early-Talent-Program--Infrastructure---Renewable-Resources_JR101589","source_url":"https://bci.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/BCI_Careers/job/Victoria-BC/Analyst--Early-Talent-Program--Infrastructure---Renewable-Resources_JR101589","source_name":"BCI public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Analyst Institutional Investing opportunity with BCI in Victoria, BC focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"About Us: With $313.7 billion of gross assets under management, as of March 31, 2026, British Columbia Investment Management Corporation (BCI) is the provider of investment management services for British Columbia’s public sector and one of the largest asset managers in Canada. BCI seeks investment opportunities around the world and across a range of asset classes that convert savings into productive capital. Our investment returns play a significant role in helping our institutional clients build a financially secure future for their beneficiaries. Headquartered in Victoria, British Columbia, and with teams spanning Vancouver, New York, London, and Mumbai. BCI integrates environmental, social, and governance (ESG) factors into all investment decisions to meet clients' risk and return requirements. Our people shape employee-focused initiatives, creating a strong culture. To learn more about our culture and values, visit our BCI Values in Action page. POSTING CLOSE DATE: October 8, 2026 Join BCI’s Infrastructure & Renewable Resources (I&RR) Early Talent Program as an Analyst in Victoria, BC. If you are a team player with excellent communication and analytical skills and an interest in investing in infrastructure, forestry, and agriculture – launch your career on the buy-side with one of Canada’s top infrastructure investors. Our 2-year program offers a competitive compensation and benefits package with annual bonus eligibility and an extensive training and development program. Based in Victoria, B.C., you will also enjoy year-round access to the outdoors in Canada's mildest climate! Ready to launch your investment career? We value diverse perspectives and recognize that some skills can be learned on the job. We encourage all candidates to apply. ABOUT BCI’s I&RR TEAM We’re one of the world's top 10 institutional infrastructure investors, managing C$36.5+ billion in AUM from our offices in Victoria, BC and London, UK. Our team invests in infrastructure, forestry, and agriculture businesses that deliver stable, long-term returns for our clients. We pursue these opportunities primarily through direct investments in private businesses, complemented by public market and debt strategies. Across our portfolio, we take an active governance approach built on trusted partnerships and long-term value creation. The Early Talent Program Designed for ambitious new graduates and early-career professionals, this two-year program will give you comprehensive exposure to institutional investing. As a member of I&RR’s investment team, you will gain hands-on experience across a wide range of industries and investing strategies. This program also offers valuable international and cross-functional exposure, including potential travel opportunities for deal execution or portfolio company engagement. Your development is central to the program – supported through a customized training program, on the job experience, a mentorship program that provide ongoing coaching and guidance, and networking opportunities with BCI professionals and industry peers. THE ROLE As an Analyst, you’ll be an integral part of our investment team contributing to (1) due diligence of prospective investments, (2) proactive engagement with portfolio companies owned by I&RR, and (3) executing on strategic initiatives across the portfolio. Investment Due Diligence Work within an integrated deal team to conduct due diligence on direct private, public, debt, or fund investments Develop financial models with sensitivity analysis to evaluate investment opportunities Collaborate with internal and external teams to support commercial, technical, ESG and other workstreams Synthesize and present findings to senior leadership in investment presentations and memos Portfolio Company Engagement Support business strategy development and budget planning for I&RR’s portfolio companies as well as addressing other pertinent issues confronting Board and management teams Monitor and report on portfolio companies’ performance, as well as support on valuations Evaluate and support strategic initiatives such as bolt-on acquisitions, divestitures, and expansion projects Strategic Initiatives Research industries, companies, and markets to support origination activities Contribute to geographic strategic reviews to support origination and portfolio initiatives Build institutional knowledge on evolving trends and investment challenges/opportunities QUALIFICATIONS Undergraduate university degree from a relevant field (Business, Finance, Economics, or equivalent) Relevant internships (new grads) or up to 3 years of experience within private equity, investment banking, management consulting, corporate M&A, investment management, or other suitable background Understanding of private market investing and strong financial modeling and analytical capabilities Excellent written and verbal communication skills A team player that thrives in a fast-pace, team-oriented environment Demonstrates natural curiosity, an inquisitive mindset, and an eagerness to learn Exhibits a high level of integrity, professionalism, and excellent interpersonal skills Beneficial but not required: Experience in or knowledge of infrastructure, forestry, or agriculture investments Additional language capabilities and/or international exposure Progress towards a relevant professional designation (e.g., CFA etc.) WHERE YOU WILL WORK This role is based in our downtown Victoria, BC office. SALARY RANGE The annualized base salary range for this Victoria-based role is CAD $97,000 to $115,000. BCI offers a competitive total rewards package, including a performance-based incentive plan, comprehensive health & dental benefits, a defined benefit pension plan, and paid time off. We pay our people competitively in the markets in which we operate and with consideration for internal equity and job structure. The base salary will consider factors such as the individual's skill set, experience, and internal equity. We aim for actual pay to be around the market median for expected performance and the upper quartile for excellent performance. Actual salaries may vary based on experience and expertise. Next Steps: To apply online, please submit your resume promptly. Applications will be actively reviewed, and those selected for an interview will be contacted. We welcome all qualified candidates who are legally authorized to work in the country where this job is located. If you do not have authorization, or if your work permit has restrictions or is due to expire within 12 months, please inform our recruitment team if shortlisted. At BCI, we value diversity and foster an inclusive culture where all employees can thrive. We are performance and client-focused, valuing integrity, and we want to know you if you share these values. We recognize that some skills can be learned on the job and encourage everyone to apply. If you require accommodations for the recruitment process, such as alternate formats of materials or accessible meeting rooms, please contact us at hr@bci.ca . To learn more about working with BCI, including our comprehensive benefits packages, our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and the recruitment process visit our BCI Careers Page . BCI does not accept unsolicited resumes or candidate submissions from third-party recruitment agencies, executive search firms, or staffing suppliers unless they have an existing contractual agreement with our organization. Our approved vendor relationships are established for particular recruitment requirements and do not extend to general job postings on our website or other platforms. Any candidate information or resumes submitted by suppliers not approved by BCI will be deemed unsolicited and will not be reviewed or considered. BCI will not be liable for any fees, commissions, or charges related to unsolicited candidate submissions or recruitment services .","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"bci:JR101589","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR101352","company_id":"bci","company_name":"BCI","title":"Associate/Senior Associate (Listed Infrastructure)","location_display":"Victoria, BC","city":"Victoria","province":"BC","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Associate","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-07-23","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":120000,"salary_max":150000,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://bci.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/BCI_Careers/job/Victoria-BC/Associate--Listed-Infrastructure-_JR101352","source_url":"https://bci.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/BCI_Careers/job/Victoria-BC/Associate--Listed-Infrastructure-_JR101352","source_name":"BCI public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Associate Institutional Investing opportunity with BCI in Victoria, BC focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"About Us: With $313.7 billion of gross assets under management, as of March 31, 2026, British Columbia Investment Management Corporation (BCI) is the provider of investment management services for British Columbia’s public sector and one of the largest asset managers in Canada. BCI seeks investment opportunities around the world and across a range of asset classes that convert savings into productive capital. Our investment returns play a significant role in helping our institutional clients build a financially secure future for their beneficiaries. Headquartered in Victoria, British Columbia, and with teams spanning Vancouver, New York, London, and Mumbai. BCI integrates environmental, social, and governance (ESG) factors into all investment decisions to meet clients' risk and return requirements. Our people shape employee-focused initiatives, creating a strong culture. To learn more about our culture and values, visit our BCI Values in Action page. Join BCI's Listed Infrastructure team at an exciting stage of growth. You'll be part of a global strategy with significant capital to deploy, backed by the scale, experience, and long-term perspective of a leading institutional investor. The role includes a performance-based incentive plan and is based in Victoria, BC, where you'll enjoy year-round access to the outdoors in Canada's mildest climate. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. POSTING CLOSE DATE: Open Until Filled THE OPPORTUNITY: The Associate/Senior Associate is a member of the team's investment group and contributes to the sourcing, evaluation, execution, and monitoring of infrastructure investments, with a focus on publicly traded infrastructure businesses. The role provides exposure to global infrastructure investment opportunities and the opportunity to work alongside experienced investors in a collaborative team environment. The ideal candidate will bring strong corporate finance and investment analysis capabilities, sound judgment, intellectual curiosity, and a long-term investment mindset. The position may be filled at either the Associate or Senior Associate level, depending on experience. WHO YOU WILL WORK WITH: On behalf of BCI’s clients, the Infrastructure & Renewable Resources (I&RR) team invests globally in infrastructure assets and businesses that provide stable long-term investment returns. BCI’s I&RR portfolio has $32+ billion in AUM and ranks as the ninth largest institutional infrastructure investor globally. The portfolio spans a range of sectors including energy, transport, utilities, and data infrastructure as well as tangible assets such as timberland and agriculture. I&RR seeks meaningful investments predominantly in private companies that allow us to pursue an active management and governance approach. The team invests in a variety of capacities in private markets including as a sole sponsor, co-sponsor, and very selectively through externally managed funds. In addition, I&RR takes positions in listed infrastructure businesses as well as debt investments as complementary strategies to private markets investments. In 2023, the I&RR team established their first international presence with the inauguration of their London, U.K. office. The new London office serves as a strong platform for the team to originate and manage investments in the U.K. and European markets, further solidifying BCI's commitment to global expansion and diversification. WHAT YOU BRING Undergraduate university degree or completion of an MBA, CFA is an asset Minimum 3+ years of experience in infrastructure investing (public or private markets), investment banking, or equity research Financial modelling, valuation, and analytical expertise Excellent communication skills, intellectual curiosity, sound judgment, and a passion for investing Ability to build effective working relationships and contribute in a collaborative team environment WHAT YOU WILL DO Conduct industry, company, and investment research across global infrastructure markets Evaluate direct investment opportunities through financial analysis, valuation, due diligence, and investment research Assess investment opportunities, including historical asset performance, competitive positioning, management quality, and key value drivers Support transaction execution, including due diligence, financial modelling, and investment recommendations Monitor portfolio investments and contribute to investment theses, performance assessments, and portfolio reviews Prepare valuation analyses and portfolio reporting materials Contribute to the development of long-term portfolio strategies and tactical investment initiatives Support sourcing, origination, and relationship-building activities across infrastructure markets Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders, including management teams, advisors, and investment partners Travel, as required, to support due diligence, transaction execution, and portfolio oversight WHERE YOU WILL WORK This role will be based in our office in downtown Victoria, BC. SALARY RANGE The annualized base salary range for this Victoria-based role is CAD $120,000 - $150,000. BCI offers a competitive total rewards package, including a performance-based incentive plan, comprehensive health & dental benefits, a defined benefit pension plan, and paid time off. We pay our people competitively in the markets in which we operate and with consideration for internal equity and job structure. The base salary will consider factors such as the individual's skill set, experience, and internal equity. We aim for actual pay to be around the market median for expected performance and the upper quartile for excellent performance. Actual salaries may vary based on experience and expertise. Next Steps: To apply online, please submit your resume promptly. Applications will be actively reviewed, and those selected for an interview will be contacted. We welcome all qualified candidates who are legally authorized to work in the country where this job is located. If you do not have authorization, or if your work permit has restrictions or is due to expire within 12 months, please inform our recruitment team if shortlisted. At BCI, we value diversity and foster an inclusive culture where all employees can thrive. We are performance and client-focused, valuing integrity, and we want to know you if you share these values. We recognize that some skills can be learned on the job and encourage everyone to apply. If you require accommodations for the recruitment process, such as alternate formats of materials or accessible meeting rooms, please contact us at hr@bci.ca . To learn more about working with BCI, including our comprehensive benefits packages, our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and the recruitment process visit our BCI Careers Page . BCI does not accept unsolicited resumes or candidate submissions from third-party recruitment agencies, executive search firms, or staffing suppliers unless they have an existing contractual agreement with our organization. Our approved vendor relationships are established for particular recruitment requirements and do not extend to general job postings on our website or other platforms. Any candidate information or resumes submitted by suppliers not approved by BCI will be deemed unsolicited and will not be reviewed or considered. BCI will not be liable for any fees, commissions, or charges related to unsolicited candidate submissions or recruitment services .","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"bci:JR101352","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"R4942","company_id":"psp-investments","company_name":"PSP Investments","title":"Senior Analyst, Canada Growth Fund Investment Management","location_display":"Montreal, QC","city":"Montreal","province":"QC","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":null,"seniority":"Analyst","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-22","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://investpsp.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/psp_careers/job/Montreal/Senior-Analyst--Canada-Growth-Fund-Investment-Management_R4942-1","source_url":"https://investpsp.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/psp_careers/job/Montreal/Senior-Analyst--Canada-Growth-Fund-Investment-Management_R4942-1","source_name":"PSP Investments public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Analyst Institutional Investing opportunity with PSP Investments in Montreal, QC.","description_text":"ABOUT US We’re one of Canada’s largest pension investors, with CAD$320.6 billion of net assets as of March 31, 2026. We invest funds for the pension plans of the federal public service, the Canadian Forces, the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Reserve Force. Headquartered in Ottawa, PSP Investments has its principal business office in Montréal and offices in New York, London and Hong Kong. Capturing and leading complex global investments requires us to work as one to seize valuable opportunities, in close collaboration with some of the world’s top companies. At PSP, you’ll join a team of motivated and engaged professionals, dedicated to propelling our organization further than ever before. In Budget 2023, the Government of Canada announced that PSP Investments would act as the independent and exclusive investment manager for the Canada Growth Fund (CGF) a $15 billion public investment vehicle that was established to support the growth of Canada’s clean economy and help to meet its national economic and climate policy goals. Following this, PSP Investments has incorporated CGF Investment Management (CGFIM) for that purpose. CGFIM is providing the full suite of investment management services to CGF covering the entire investment process pursuant to an Investment Management Agreement (IMA). ABOUT THE TEAM The Canada Growth Fund Investment Management (CGFIM) team is a new team created within PSP to manage the C$15bn Canada Growth Fund. CGF’s mandate is to catalyze substantial private sector investment in Canadian low-carbon projects, technologies, businesses, and supply chains by deploying innovative funding structures that help mitigate certain risks and uncertainties inherent to investing in the low-carbon economy. CGF is investing in Canadian projects and companies across themes such as carbon capture, hydrogen, renewable natural gas, clean technology, and critical minerals. Size of the team: The team currently consists of approximately 33 professionals and is growing to support the execution of CGF’s mandate. ABOUT YOUR ROLE As Senior Analyst, Canada Growth Fund Investment Management , you will be actively participating in the energy transition in Canada, deploying and managing CGF’s capital, shaping strategy and executing investments with a focus on low carbon supply chains including critical minerals. Responsibilities include: Assess investment opportunities in the critical minerals commodities and technologies (including relevant regulatory and policy frameworks), execute transactions, and be involved in post-investment asset management Actively participate in the mining industry in Canada by developing relationships with strategics and investors, attend industry/banker meetings, build sector knowledge, and maintain ongoing market awareness Analyze and review key trends in mining as it pertains to the energy transition and domestic supply chains, conduct ad hoc deep dive research, prepare supporting analysis, interact with industry experts Research relevant public information, keep abreast of important industry developments and publications and disseminate relevant information to the rest of the team Participate in the investment appraisal process (build detailed operational and financial models for upstream, midstream or downstream mining and / or industrial assets, determine and substantiate key valuation assumptions, conduct sensitivity analyses on main value drivers) Actively contribute to due diligence activities conducted on potential opportunities, including coordination and review of the work performed by third-party advisors (commercial, environmental, technical, legal, financing, accounting, tax, environmental, etc.) Form a view on an appropriate expected return, commensurate with the level of risk embedded in the underwritten business plan, through the lens of CGF’s mandate Assist deal teams in the determination of material ESG factors and calculation of impact metrics, including avoided emissions and economic benefits associated with transactions Participate in the preparation of investment memorandums and presentation of recommendations to the investment committees Develop new and cultivate existing network of industry contacts to improve access to information for the entire team Note: The position requires travel within Canada and potentially internationally. WHAT YOU’LL NEED Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field. Master’s degree in a relevant field, an asset Professional designation such as CPA ,MBA CFA or CBV, considered an asset One (1) to four (4) years of relevant experience within the mining industry with a focus on mining investing and/or investment banking/corporate finance/transaction services Solid understanding of financial statements, excellent analytical skills, and sound critical judgement Being a team player who enjoys a high-performance culture Strong interpersonal skills and ability to communicate effectively A respect for differences of opinion and an inclusive mindset High level of proficiency with Microsoft Office Tools (more specifically Excel, Word and PowerPoint) and financial analytical tools and databases such as Capital IQ and Bloomberg Good communications skills in English and French (or willingness to learn) (regular interactions in English with investment partners based outside of Quebec. Example: peers, bankers, brokerage firms, etc. and PSP employees in our offices in Hong Kong, London and New York, and interactions in French with employees in our local offices in Montreal and Ottawa) We offer a tailored employee experience and competitive total rewards and benefits package* designed to attract and retain global diverse talent, reward performance, and reinforce business strategies and priorities. Beyond salary and incentive pay eligibility, you have access to: Investment in career development Comprehensive group insurance plans Competitive pension plans Unlimited access to virtual healthcare services and wellness programs Gender-inclusive paid family leave policy : up to 26 weeks for primary caregivers, 5 weeks for secondary caregivers A personalized family-building support , from pre-pregnancy to menopause, with available financial assistance Vacation days available on day one with additional days on milestone service anniversaries, and summer Friday afternoons off A hybrid work model that includes four in-office days, Monday through Thursday The opportunity to work temporarily from another location in accordance with the applicable policy *Benefits package may vary based on your employee type. At PSP Investments, we aim to provide a workplace where everyone feels valued, safe, respected and empowered to grow. As part of this leadership commitment, we strongly encourage applications from all qualified applicants and strive to offer an inclusive and accessible candidate experience. If you require any accommodation for any part of the recruitment process, please let us know. Visit us on www.investpsp.com/en/ Follow us on LinkedIn #LI-AM1","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"psp-investments:R4942","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR100894","company_id":"aimco","company_name":"AIMCo","title":"Student, Real Estate (May 2027)","location_display":"Calgary, AB","city":"Calgary","province":"AB","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Real Estate Investing","specialization":"Real Estate","seniority":"Student","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-08-27","application_deadline":"2026-10-01","salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--Real-Estate--May-2027-_JR100894","source_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Student--Real-Estate--May-2027-_JR100894","source_name":"AIMCo public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Student Real Estate Investing opportunity with AIMCo in Calgary, AB focused on Real Estate.","description_text":"CLOSING DATE: October 1, 2026 Opportunity Are you looking to complement your academic knowledge with professional ‘real world’ experience? Are you a purpose-driven individual who wants to contribute to your community? Do you enthusiastically follow financial markets or seek out emerging trends in technology? If so, a student position at AIMCo might be the opportunity for you to gain the experience you need to launch your career while contributing to the financial security of hundreds of thousands of Albertans. Highly successful students at AIMCo share many of the same characteristics. They are intellectually curious, diligent, and responsible, with a desire to enhance their finance, data, programming, and communications skills. They take advantage of their time at AIMCo by building relationships with our talented workforce and each other. The Real Estate Analytics, Research, & Governance (ARG) team is responsible for capturing and maintaining all data derived from the real estate portfolio – and turning that into meaningful analytical insights to make informed investment decisions. The team provides a strategic research lens to the investment team and is responsible for investment process governance practices to ensure strong decision-making. ARG has full coverage of the global real estate portfolio. As the Student, Real Estate, you will have gained a working knowledge of Canadian and Foreign Real Estate Investment Portfolios. ***Job Posting will expire at 11:59pm MT on September 30, 2026*** Responsibilities: Collecting and maintaining investment and portfolio-level data across the Canada, US, and European regions. Conducting analysis on the existing portfolio to understand various risk metrics and exposures. Observing the real estate investment committee and learning investment process governance. Participating in several ad-hoc projects to gain working knowledge of AIMCo’s real estate asset class. Contributing to the maintenance and accuracy of internal real estate management systems (YARDI) Creating Real Estate Investment charts/tables for Portfolio presentations Our Ideal Candidate: Undergraduate Student enrolled in Commerce/Business, Finance, Economics, Computer Science with a passion for Real Estate Proficient with Microsoft Applications (Excel, PowerPoint, Word, Outlook) Exceptional attention to detail, and an ability to manage multiple tasks and work under pressure to meet deadlines Strong research, analytical and problem-solving abilities Knowledge of Real Estate would be considered an asset Thrives under pressure and enjoys contributing to team goals and collaborating Demonstrates a strong commitment to AIMCo’s core values of excellence, transparency, humility, integrity and collaboration, and inspires the same in others Success Measures: Success at the end of your term will be determined by the undertaking and completion of specified daily tasks while collaborating with the team, sharing your ideas, and contributing to ongoing projects. You will take advantage of your summer at AIMCo by building connections across the organization. #LI-ET1 Next Steps We are excited to meet you. Please submit your resume or CV to be considered for this opportunity. Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis and we will be in touch with any questions. Final candidates will be asked to undergo a security screening, which includes a credit bureau and a criminal record investigation, the results of which must be acceptable to AIMCo. ALERT - Be on the lookout for AIMCo career opportunities advertised through third parties that request an application fee or too much information. To verify, all opportunities are posted on aimco.ca/jobs At AIMCo, we draw upon the differences in who we are, where we come from and the way we think to deliver results for the Albertans who rely on us. We offer an inclusive, modern workplace where well-being is prioritized, and colleagues are enabled to do their best work. Our team members are motivated by our purpose and committed to creating long-term value for our clients and their beneficiaries.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"aimco:JR100894","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR100898","company_id":"aimco","company_name":"AIMCo","title":"Co-op, Fixed Income (May 2027)","location_display":"Calgary, AB","city":"Calgary","province":"AB","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Public Credit / Fixed Income","seniority":"Student","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Co-op","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-08-27","application_deadline":"2026-10-01","salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Co-op--Fixed-Income--May-2027-_JR100898","source_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Co-op--Fixed-Income--May-2027-_JR100898","source_name":"AIMCo public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Co-op Student Institutional Investing opportunity with AIMCo in Calgary, AB focused on Public Credit / Fixed Income.","description_text":"CLOSING DATE: October 1, 2026 Opportunity Are you looking for an opportunity to gain exposure to fixed income portfolio management, quantitative research, and investment analysis? AIMCo’s Fixed Income group manages several different short-, mid-, and long-term portfolios for our clients and provides active management of money market and fixed income investments. The Co-op, Fixed Income will assist the department in its objective to add value relative to benchmarks through interest rate forecasting, term structure weighting, sector weighting and security selection. Note: This is a 4-month, full-time term starting in May 2027. ***Job Posting will expire at 11:59pm MT on September 30, 2026*** Responsibilities: Contributing to the Fixed Income team’s development of quantitative statistical models, back-testing, curve building, or other quantitative analysis. Determining which factor investing models can be applied to bond or credit portfolio management. Collaborating with the Fixed Income team to determine what tools can be used to improve fixed income processes. Improving and creation of new management reports used for more informed investment decision making. Leverage AI-enabled tools to enhance research, portfolio monitoring, reporting, and operational efficiency. Demonstrate proficiency in AI-assisted analytical workflows and maintain awareness of emerging technologies relevant to investment management. Maintaining and updating Fixed Income databases and SharePoint site. Working with the reporting group on existing reports or creating new reports for Fixed Income team. Assisting in the quarterly client reporting process. Supporting and working on documentation of existing high-level data and process flows. Ideal Candidate Qualifications: Currently enrolled in undergraduate or graduate studies in a quantitative discipline including finance, economics, engineering, computer science, mathematics, physics, or related field combined with a demonstrated passion for investments. Must be part of a work experience program with a post-secondary institution (Ex: Co-op). Strong Python programming skills are required. Experience using data analysis and scientific computing libraries (e.g., pandas, NumPy, SciPy) is considered an asset. Experience working with large and complex datasets using Python through internships, research projects, or coursework. Experience with SQL, VBA or other programming languages is an asset. Understanding of financial markets, particularly the fixed income market. Knowledge of financial instruments such as bonds, derivatives, and money market instruments is a plus. An interest in Fixed Income quantitative trading and analysis. Prior experience with conducting financial research, preferably using Bloomberg or Capital IQ is an asset. Advanced proficiency level with Microsoft Applications (Excel, PowerPoint, Word, Outlook, SharePoint) Strong attention to detail with strong research, critical thinking, and analytical skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work under pressure and meet deadlines while working independently and collaboratively. Self-motivated and proactive. The ideal candidate should be eager to learn, able to take initiative, and willing to go the extra mile to deliver results. CFA Level I (or working towards it) Demonstrates a strong commitment to AIMCo’s core values of excellence, transparency, humility, integrity and collaboration, and inspiring the same in others. Success Measures: During your time with the Fixed Income team, you will have developed an understanding of the variety of fixed income products AIMCo holds while working collaboratively and effectively with the team to champion continuous improvement and support the team on identifying opportunities that enhance data management and investment analysis processes. #LI-ET1 Next Steps We are excited to meet you. Please submit your resume or CV to be considered for this opportunity. Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis and we will be in touch with any questions. Final candidates will be asked to undergo a security screening, which includes a credit bureau and a criminal record investigation, the results of which must be acceptable to AIMCo. ALERT - Be on the lookout for AIMCo career opportunities advertised through third parties that request an application fee or too much information. To verify, all opportunities are posted on aimco.ca/jobs At AIMCo, we draw upon the differences in who we are, where we come from and the way we think to deliver results for the Albertans who rely on us. We offer an inclusive, modern workplace where well-being is prioritized, and colleagues are enabled to do their best work. Our team members are motivated by our purpose and committed to creating long-term value for our clients and their beneficiaries.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"aimco:JR100898","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR100892","company_id":"aimco","company_name":"AIMCo","title":"Co-op, Renewable Resources (8 Months)","location_display":"Calgary, AB","city":"Calgary","province":"AB","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Student","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Co-op","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-08-27","application_deadline":"2026-10-01","salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Co-op--Renewable-Resources--8-Months-_JR100892","source_url":"https://aimco.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/AIMCoCareers/job/Calgary/Co-op--Renewable-Resources--8-Months-_JR100892","source_name":"AIMCo public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Co-op Student Institutional Investing opportunity with AIMCo in Calgary, AB focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"CLOSING DATE: October 1, 2026 Opportunity AIMCo’s Renewable Resources group is seeking a thoughtful and ambitious student to join the team in May 2027 for an eight-month term. The Renewable Resources program comprises a global portfolio of land-centric, high-quality timberland and agricultural assets that are characterized by their low correlation to traditional asset classes, inflation-hedging qualities, and a strong match with client time horizons. Renewable resources assets serve to provide capital preservation, current yield, and real asset appreciation. The Renewable Resources program is concentrated in developed market countries with an opportunistic view on emerging market exposure. Flexibility is ingrained into the Renewable Resources mandate, which allows the team to maximize long-term value by optimizing portfolio assets between timberland, agriculture, and strategic investments along the value chain. Highly successful students at AIMCo share many of the same characteristics. They are intellectually curious, diligent, and responsible, with a desire to enhance their finance, data, programming, and communications skills. They take advantage of their time at AIMCo by building relationships with our talented workforce and each other. As a Student, Renewable Resources, you will work closely with investment professionals in the group on financial analysis at the project and portfolio level, monitoring performance of existing investments, undertaking due diligence on new investments and developing models and tools for conducting such analyses. Your attention to detail, ability to work under pressure, and commitment to excellence in financial modelling, market research, and investment analysis will form the foundation of your contributions to AIMCo. Note: This is an 8-month, full-time term from May 2027 through December 2027. ***Job Posting will expire at 11:59pm MT on September 30, 2026*** Responsibilities: Supporting the analysis and execution of investment opportunities across a variety of renewable resource sectors and geographies Assisting in the management of the due diligence process, building and working with complex financial models, investment structuring and financing Developing recommendations and approval materials clearly outlining potential investment opportunities, including expected risks and returns, as well as detailed market and asset-level considerations Monitoring current investments’ financial and operating results Participate in asset management initiatives for existing portfolio investments Performing analysis detailing the state of the market for investments to aid and support senior investment professionals’ understanding of market developments Support the completion of global macro research projects to help inform future portfolio construction Supporting the Renewable Resources team on projects to improve the dissemination and organization of information and other administrative endeavors Ideal Candidate Qualifications: Completion of second or third-year undergraduate studies in Finance/Quantitative fields (i.e. Finance, Business, Economics, Accounting, Mathematics, Engineering, or Computer Science) Proven track record of outstanding academic achievement and performance Motivated self-starter who can work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced and dynamic team environment High attention to detail and an ability to manage multiple tasks and work under pressure to meet deadlines Exposure within corporate finance, or business development within renewable resources finance, private investments, project finance, agriculture or forestry is an asset Interest in the pursuit of a professional designation (e.g. CFA, CPA, CAIA) is an asset Intellectual curiosity and willingness to learn more about renewable resources is essential Able to keep composed under pressure and prioritize multiple deadlines Strong analytical skills and problem-solving experience are an asset Strong technical skills in Excel, Word, and PowerPoint are required Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present quantitative and qualitative topics to a wide audience clearly and compellingly, are required Prior work-related or academic experience using Bloomberg, Capital IQ, Factset will be viewed favorably Demonstrates a strong commitment to AIMCo’s core values of excellence, transparency, humility, integrity and collaboration, and inspires the same in others Success Measures: Success at the end of your term will be determined by your ability to seek out learning opportunities and become involved in multiple projects, tasks, responsibilities, and investments. You will have developed an increased understanding of investment concepts and market knowledge and a new appreciation of finance and investment management. A student who goes above and beyond expectations will participate in multiple investment opportunities and add value to team projects and initiatives. #LI-ET1 Next Steps We are excited to meet you. Please submit your resume or CV to be considered for this opportunity. Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis and we will be in touch with any questions. Final candidates will be asked to undergo a security screening, which includes a credit bureau and a criminal record investigation, the results of which must be acceptable to AIMCo. ALERT - Be on the lookout for AIMCo career opportunities advertised through third parties that request an application fee or too much information. To verify, all opportunities are posted on aimco.ca/jobs At AIMCo, we draw upon the differences in who we are, where we come from and the way we think to deliver results for the Albertans who rely on us. We offer an inclusive, modern workplace where well-being is prioritized, and colleagues are enabled to do their best work. Our team members are motivated by our purpose and committed to creating long-term value for our clients and their beneficiaries.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"aimco:JR100892","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"JR102503","company_id":"hoopp","company_name":"HOOPP","title":"Senior Associate, HOOPP Capital Partners","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Private Credit","seniority":"Associate","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-08-11","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":98000,"salary_max":148000,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://hoopp.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/HOOPP/job/Toronto-Ontario-Canada/Sr-Associate--HOOPP-Capital-Partners_JR102503","source_url":"https://hoopp.wd10.myworkdayjobs.com/HOOPP/job/Toronto-Ontario-Canada/Sr-Associate--HOOPP-Capital-Partners_JR102503","source_name":"HOOPP public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Associate Institutional Investing opportunity with HOOPP in Toronto, ON focused on Private Credit.","description_text":"Why you’ll love working here: high-performance, people-focused culture our commitment that equity, diversity, and inclusion are fundamental to our work environment and business success, which helps employees feel valued and empowered to be their authentic selves learning and development initiatives, including workshops, Speaker Series events and access to LinkedIn Learning, that support employees’ career growth membership in HOOPP’s world class defined benefit pension plan, which can serve as an important part of your retirement security competitive, 100% company-paid extended health and dental benefits for permanent employees, including coverage supporting our team's diversity and mental health (e.g., gender affirmation, fertility and drug treatment, psychological support benefits of $2,500 per year, parental leave top-up, and a health spending account). optional post-retirement health and dental benefits subsidized at 50% yoga classes, meditation workshops, nutritional consultations, and wellness seminars the opportunity to make a difference and help take care of those who care for us, by providing a financially secure retirement for Ontario healthcare workers Job Summary As a Senior Associate within HOOPP Capital Partners, you will focus primarily on venture capital & growth equity, and gain hands-on exposure to the full investment lifecycle across venture capital and growth equity, including fund commitments, co-investments, direct investments, portfolio monitoring, and market research. You will also have exposure to other private capital strategies within HOOPP Capital Partners, and may have opportunities to support the execution and management of selected private equity or private credit investments within the portfolio. This is a foundational role designed for intellectually curious, motivated individuals who are eager to contribute to help advance HOOPP’s venture capital and growth equity strategy over time. The role offers strong development opportunities with increasing responsibility based on performance, including exposure to leading venture capital fund managers, growth-stage companies, internal investment teams, and cross-functional partners across HOOPP. What you will do: Investment Execution Support the evaluation and execution of venture capital and growth equity fund commitments, co-investments, and direct investments Conduct due diligence on potential investment opportunities, including company, market, competitive, financial, operational, technological, legal, tax, and risk considerations Build and maintain dynamic, user-friendly financial models for valuation, return analysis, scenario analysis, and portfolio monitoring Prepare and contribute to investment memos, committee materials, market maps, fund diligence materials, and other internal investment documentation Assist in evaluating deal structuring, investment terms, fund documents, and transaction implications Support the development and maintenance of a robust investment pipeline by screening relevant opportunities and tracking market activity Portfolio and Relationship Management Monitor financial and operational performance of venture capital and growth equity investments, including both fund investments and direct/co-investments Assist with periodic valuations, performance attribution, investment reporting, and portfolio review materials Support analysis of follow-on investment opportunities, financing alternatives, exit considerations, and other portfolio company developments Help manage investment relationships with fund managers, company management teams, intermediaries, consultants, and other external partners Stay abreast of developments in venture capital, growth equity, technology markets, regulation, and relevant legal, tax, and risk matters Strategic and Internal Initiatives Contribute to research and analysis on investment themes, sectors, structures, and emerging technologies Support the continued evolution of HOOPP’s venture capital and growth equity strategy in collaboration with senior team members Engage with internal stakeholders across investments, legal, tax, accounting, operations, risk, and other teams to support transaction execution and portfolio management Collaborate with HOOPP’s AI Lab and broader internal partners to share insights, enhance analysis, and identify opportunities to apply technology and AI tools to investment processes Contribute to team initiatives, including process improvements, knowledge sharing, portfolio-level strategy, risk management, and sustainability-related work What you bring: 3–5 years of experience in venture capital, growth equity, investment banking, private equity, or a related investment role University degree in Finance, Commerce, Economics, Engineering, Computer Science, or another relevant field, with strong academic performance Demonstrated interest in venture capital, growth equity, technology investing, innovation, and private markets Strong financial modeling, valuation, business analysis, and due diligence skills Ability to conduct rigorous market, company, sector, and fund manager research Strong written and oral communication skills, with the ability to synthesize complex ideas clearly and concisely Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel, PowerPoint, and Word; experience with Capital IQ, Bloomberg, Pitchbook, Preqin, or other data and analytics platforms is considered an asset Demonstrated ability to leverage AI tools to enhance financial analysis, data synthesis, research, and productivity Understanding of current trends across technology subsectors such as AI, enterprise SaaS, fintech, digital health, life sciences, and other emerging areas is considered an asset Curious mindset, strong attention to detail, sound judgment, and a proactive attitude High integrity, professionalism, and team orientation Strong collaboration and relationship management skills, including the ability to work effectively with internal partners and external stakeholders The expected annual base salary range for this role is: $98,000 - $148,000 CAD The actual base salary offered to the successful candidate may vary based on multiple factors including, but not limited to, individual's expertise and level of experience applicable to the role they are being offered. This role is eligible to participate in discretionary incentive plan(s), subject to the terms and conditions of the applicable incentive plan text. This job posting is for a newly created role. HOOPP may use artificial intelligence tools to assist in screening, assessing and selecting applicants for this position. These tools support our recruitment process but do not replace human judgment and decision-making.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"hoopp:JR102503","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"R26-138","company_id":"imco","company_name":"IMCO","title":"Analyst, Real Estate (Fixed-term contract)","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Real Estate Investing","specialization":"Real Estate","seniority":"Analyst","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Contract","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-09-28","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":95000,"salary_max":120000,"salary_currency":"CAD","salary_period":"year","application_url":"https://imcoinvest.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/IMCO/job/Toronto---16-York-St/Analyst--Real-Estate--Fixed-term-contract-_R26-138-1","source_url":"https://imcoinvest.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/IMCO/job/Toronto---16-York-St/Analyst--Real-Estate--Fixed-term-contract-_R26-138-1","source_name":"IMCO public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Contract Analyst Real Estate Investing opportunity with IMCO in Toronto, ON focused on Real Estate.","description_text":"At IMCO, our talent is among the best! IMCO offers a uniquely stimulating and rewarding environment where you can help build and drive organizational transformation, all while seeking to challenge yourself, learn, and grow your career. Our culture is built on collaboration and passion, with a shared commitment to delivering lasting value to the clients we serve. Located in downtown Toronto, our vision is to be the partner of choice for Ontario’s public sector funds and to build a high-performing, value-driven asset management firm. This job posting is for an existing vacancy. If you are ready to deliver best-in-class service and join a collaborative, motivated and fun team of professionals, IMCO offers the opportunity to do impactful work and broaden your expertise. If you’re looking to use your expertise to drive strategic outcomes, we’d love to hear from you. ‎ **This is a Fixed-term contract that will end in December 2027** The successful incumbent will work under the direction of the Principal, Real Estate. The Analyst is part of the broader Investments team and is primarily responsible for supporting team members across the Real Estate asset class as it pertains to the management of the Real Estate investment portfolio. The role will primarily support ongoing portfolio management and reporting, the asset management of select Canadian properties, and broader real estate portfolio initiatives. It may also include investment analysis and research related to new investment opportunities and potential dispositions. As a Member of Our Team, You Will: Develop, generate, and collate analysis using various sources for investment and portfolio management, and to satisfy board and client reporting requirements. Support the ongoing development and enhancement of departmental applications, including report creation, systems review and implementations and process enhancements using AI. Ensure information in portfolio management applications and files is current, accurate, and readily accessible. Support asset monitoring throughout the investment lifecycle. Apply investment management knowledge to support the Real Estate team through research and analysis that informs strategies to improve the portfolio’s risk-return profile. Conduct research and analysis on a broad range of topics to support investment decision-making across the Real Estate asset class. Assist the Real Estate team in the due diligence process and preparation of investment reports and presentation materials. Apply sound investment and Real Estate specific knowledge and experience to build and analyze complex financial models. What do you need to succeed? University degree in Business or a related discipline, CFA Charterholder/candidacy or AACI Designation/candidacy is an asset. One to two years of relevant work experience in real estate investing and/or investment banking is preferred. Excellent quantitative, analytical, financial modeling, problem-solving and researching skills with strong attention to detail. Strong proficiency of Microsoft Applications including Excel, PowerPoint and Word. Experience with Argus Enterprise and related real estate tools is an asset. Ability to consistently deliver quality outputs, with an ability to work to tight deadlines and the capability to prioritize and handle multiple projects and ad-hoc requests simultaneously. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to interact with colleagues at all levels and cultivate key partnerships to work collaboratively with internal and external stakeholders. Strong written and oral communication skills with the ability to explain complex issues in a clear and compelling manner and present information to internal stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to work independently, be proactive and take initiative to understand, support and implement goals and objectives. ‎ The base salary range for this position is CAD $95,000.00 - $120,000.00. The placement within the range is determined by the range of market pay for the specific position, as well as the candidate's knowledge, skillset and experience relative to the requirements of the position and to internal peers. As a candidate, you are encouraged to ask compensation related questions and have an open dialogue with your recruiter who can provide you with the specific details for this position. ‎ We thank all applicants for their interest. Only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Our hybrid work model prioritizes an office-first approach, encouraging employees to make the most of our collaborative workspace at 16 York Street, Suite 2400, Toronto, ON M5J 0E6. This welcoming environment fosters teamwork, connection, and professional growth. While flexibility remains a key component of our model, we believe that regular in-office engagement enhances productivity and strengthens our culture. Our approach supports a fulfilling lifestyle that balances professional ambition with personal wellbeing. IMCO is committed to providing accommodation for people with disabilities throughout the recruitment process. If you require support, please let us know and we will work with you to meet your needs. Artificial intelligence (AI) tools may be used to support parts of our recruitment process, such as screening and assessments. However, all hiring decisions are made by our recruitment team. Candidates being considered for this position will be required to undergo background screening.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"imco:R26-138","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"},{"external_job_id":"R2047917","company_id":"brookfield-asset-management","company_name":"Brookfield Asset Management","title":"Vice President","location_display":"Toronto, ON","city":"Toronto","province":"ON","country":"Canada","workplace_type":null,"category":"Institutional Investing","specialization":"Infrastructure","seniority":"Vice President","employment_type":"Full-time","program_type":"Full-time","term_start":null,"term_end":null,"term_length_months":null,"date_posted":"2026-08-26","application_deadline":null,"salary_min":null,"salary_max":null,"salary_currency":null,"salary_period":null,"application_url":"https://brookfield.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/brookfield/job/Toronto-Ontario/Vice-President_R2047917-1","source_url":"https://brookfield.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/brookfield/job/Toronto-Ontario/Vice-President_R2047917-1","source_name":"Brookfield Asset Management public careers site","status":"active","summary":"Vice President Institutional Investing opportunity with Brookfield Asset Management in Toronto, ON focused on Infrastructure.","description_text":"Location Brookfield Place - 181 Bay Street Business - Infrastructure Brookfield Infrastructure Group is one of Brookfield’s primary operating groups. The Infrastructure Group is one of the world’s largest infrastructure investors, owning and operating critical assets across the transport, utilities, energy, and data infrastructure sectors. The Group operates and manages approximately $191 billion of assets owned through its private funds and publicly listed entity, Brookfield Infrastructure Partners. Our portfolio of assets facilitate the movement and storage of energy, water, freight, passengers and data, and are located in North and South America, Europe and the Asia Pacific regions. For more information, visit: https://www.brookfield.com/our-businesses/infrastructure Brookfield Culture Brookfield has a unique and dynamic culture. We seek team members who have a long-term focus and whose values align with our Attributes of a Brookfield Leader: Entrepreneurial, Collaborative and Disciplined. Brookfield is committed to the development of our people through challenging work assignments and exposure to diverse businesses. Job Description The Vice President will be part of the team responsible for originating and executing M&A activity for BIG’s equity strategies, the “Investments” team. Relevant responsibilities will primarily be securing debt financing to support M&A activity including (i) providing structuring guidance (RFPs, term sheets, debt documentation, credit rating analysis etc.), (ii) running processes to secure committed financing, (iii) managing syndication processes (including working with investment banks, law firms, lenders and prospective investors), and (iv) proactively working with various internal teams to analyze / optimize the capital structure for both potential acquisitions and existing investments. In summary, the Vice President will be integral in all aspects of deal structuring, deal execution, lender / investor relationship management, as well as various ad hoc projects. Reporting Sit on the investment team and report to Managing Director, Investments (based in Toronto) and work closely with the infrastructure investment team Responsibilities Will be a key member of the acquisition financing team responsible for sourcing and structuring debt financing to support Brookfield’s global infrastructure investment initiatives Work alongside deal teams to analyze, select and implement the optimal capital structure for new investments Assist in the management of all aspects of structuring, negotiating, syndicating and documenting a new financing (including assessing reasonability of proposals, and providing recommendations to senior management) Manage the syndication process, produce credit rating materials, syndication/sales force materials, and draft internal credit documentation Work with and maintain positive relationships with banks and other financial institutions, credit rating agencies, investors, lawyers, and other external advisors Expected to be an internal expert and resource regarding broad bank / debt capital market conditions, market developments relevant to our business etc. Design tailored risk management strategies (including FX and interest rate exposure) for new acquisitions and portfolio companies in conjunction with treasury team Identify opportunities to optimize capital structures and add value through financing initiatives Interface with the broader BIG capital markets and treasury team (and Brookfield capital markets leaders) regarding capital markets strategies, banking relationships, hedging etc. Skills and Experience Requirements: Role Specific: 7-10 years of experience predominately in investment banking (debt advisory or capital markets preferred but not required), private credit, direct lending, or similar role Direct experience in origination, structuring and execution of debt transactions in the infrastructure sector Experience in managing financing and syndication processes General: Ability to work in a dynamic, global team and adapt quickly to changing priorities Analytic and strategic thinker with the ability to assess complex situations and make effective recommendations Excellent organizational skills and ability to manage priorities and meet timelines Proactive self-starter who can handle pressure effectively and has experience working with senior management teams Strong interpersonal and communication skills (oral and written) with a strength in dealing with a wide variety of individuals at various levels within and outside of the organization Team-oriented with a demonstrated commitment to shared success above any personal accomplishment or recognition Position Opening Reason: New Position Brookfield is committed to maintaining a Positive Work Environment that is safe, respectful; our shared success depends on it. We do not tolerate workplace discrimination, violence or harassment. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer and make employment decisions based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, without regard to any characteristic protected by applicable law. Applicant information is collected and handled in accordance with our Applicant Privacy Notice. As part of this commitment, we provide barrier-free and accessible employment practices in accordance with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA) and applicable human rights legislation. If you require a Human Rights Code-protected accommodation at any stage of the recruitment process, please let us know when contacted, and we will work with you to meet your needs.","description_status":"verified","description_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","source_record_id":"brookfield-asset-management:R2047917","data_quality_notes":"Description establishes direct investment research, underwriting, execution, selection, allocation or portfolio-management responsibility. Career-path classification depends on metadata or description text.","last_verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T13:09:54.056Z"}]$jobs$::jsonb)
